        <h4>Poetry</h4>
        <div class="breaker"></div>
<div class="articletext">
<h1>The First Practice</h1>
<h3 class="byline">By David S. Pointer</h3>
<p>The coach poured the<br>
extra balls out of a<br>
red drawstring bucket<br>
bag, then the kids took<br>
the mini-field forever<br>
shagging long, left, right<br>
foul plus one bouncing<br>
blast over the billboard<br>
forest where mushroom<br>
flies and fungus gnats<br>
hovered over the ball<br>
until all the fielders<br>
arrived to search deep<br>
into the dark higher homer<br>
power perimeter grass<br>
just one little league<br>
long ball game away</p>
</div>
        <p><em>&mdash;November  3, 2010</em></p>
                                 
    </div>
    <div id="printfooter">
        <h3>About the author</h3>
        <p><strong>David S. Pointer</strong> lives in Murfreesboro, Tennessee. His latest poetry chapbook is <cite>Warhammer Piano Bar</cite> from Thunderclap Press available at <a href="https://www.lulu.com/product/paperback/warhammer-piano-bar/11168456?productTrackingContext=search_results/search_shelf/center/2">Lulu.com</a>. He has poetry forthcoming at <cite>Skive Magazine</cite>, <cite>J Journal: New Writings on Justice</cite>, and <cite>Chiron Review</cite>.</p>
